IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Part 5 Division 2: s 155B (debarment for default of a relevant requirement), s 155C (disqualification
-- under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005), s 155D (disqualification under the VCC Act), s 155E (debarment under the VCC Act).
-- The Registrar, the Court and the Minister appear only as what they mean to the individual.
-- JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say. A bar is named as a bar: JUST TRUE means "barred".

§ `Section 155B: debarment for default of a relevant requirement of this Act`

DECLARE `s 155B(10) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1) where the Registrar is satisfied that a company is in default in relation to a relevant requirement, the Registrar may make a debarment order
-- against a person who, at the time, is a director or secretary of the company.
-- src:12703 | 155B.—(1) Where the Registrar is satisfied that a company is in
-- src:12704 | default in relation to a relevant requirement of this Act, the Registrar
-- src:12705 | may make a debarment order against any person who, at the time the
-- src:12706 | order is made, is a director or secretary of the company.
@ref s 155B(1) (src:12703-12706)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is in default in relation to a relevant requirement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is, at the time the order is made, a director or secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(1) the Registrar may make a debarment order against the person` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is in default in relation to a relevant requirement of this Act` AND `the person is, at the time the order is made, a director or secretary of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Registrar is satisfied that a company is in default ..., the Registrar may make a debarment order against any person who, at the time the order is made, is a director or secretary of the company" -- a "where" gate (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)) that fails; a "may" with a "where" gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

-- (6) the Registrar must not make the order unless (a) the default has persisted for a continuous period of 3 months or more while the person was director or secretary
-- and (b) the Registrar sent notice not less than 14 days before, giving an opportunity to show cause.
-- src:12749 | (6) The Registrar must not make a debarment order under
-- src:12750 | subsection (1) —
-- src:12752 | (a) unless the default in relation to a relevant requirement of
-- src:12753 | this Act has persisted for a continuous period of 3 months
-- src:12754 | or more and the person was a director or secretary of the
-- src:12755 | company during that period; and
-- src:12757 | (b) unless the Registrar has, not less than 14 days before the
-- src:12758 | order is made, sent the director or secretary concerned a
-- src:12759 | notice of the Registrar’s intention to make a debarment
-- src:12760 | order under subsection (1) specifying the default in relation
-- src:12761 | to the relevant requirement of this Act for which the
-- src:12762 | debarment order is proposed to be made and giving the
-- src:12767 | director or secretary an opportunity to show cause why the
-- src:12768 | debarment order should not be made.
@ref s 155B(6) (src:12749-12768)
GIVEN `the date the default began` IS A DATE
      `the date the order is to be made` IS A DATE
      `the person was a director or secretary of the company during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the Registrar sent the director or secretary a notice of the Registrar's intention to make a debarment order` IS A DATE
      `the notice specified the default and gave the director or secretary an opportunity to show cause why the debarment order should not be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(6) the subsection bars the Registrar from making a debarment order against the person` MEANS
    IF    `the date the order is to be made` AT LEAST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the default began` 3 Months
      AND `the person was a director or secretary of the company during that period`
      AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the Registrar sent the director or secretary a notice of the Registrar's intention to make a debarment order` `the date the order is to be made` 14 Days
      AND `the notice specified the default and gave the director or secretary an opportunity to show cause why the debarment order should not be made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must not make a debarment order under subsection (1) -- (a) unless the default ... has persisted for a continuous period of 3 months or more ...; and (b) unless the Registrar has, not less than 14 days before the order is made, sent ... a notice" -- both "unless" gates are met
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:12772 | (7) The Registrar must, in determining whether to make a
-- src:12773 | debarment order, consider any representation from the director or
-- src:12774 | secretary made pursuant to the notice under subsection (6)(b).
@ref s 155B(7) (src:12772-12774)
GIVEN `the director or secretary made a representation pursuant to the notice under subsection (6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(7) the Registrar must consider the representation in determining whether to make a debarment order` MEANS
    IF `the director or secretary made a representation pursuant to the notice under subsection (6)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must ... consider any representation from the director or secretary made pursuant to the notice" -- a scope limit with no "only": with no representation there is none to consider

-- (3) the order applies from the date it is made and continues in force until the Registrar cancels or suspends it; (5) a suspension on conditions operates so long as the person fulfils them.
-- src:12742 | (5) Where the Registrar imposes conditions on the suspension of a
-- src:12743 | debarment order under subsection (4), the suspension of the
-- src:12744 | debarment order operates so long as that person fulfils and
-- src:12745 | continues to fulfil all such conditions imposed by the Registrar.
@ref s 155B(5) (src:12742-12745)
GIVEN `the person fulfils and continues to fulfil all the conditions the Registrar imposed on the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(5) the suspension of the debarment order operates` MEANS
    IF `the person fulfils and continues to fulfil all the conditions the Registrar imposed on the suspension`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the suspension of the debarment order operates so long as that person fulfils and continues to fulfil all such conditions" -- a "so long as" condition that fails

-- src:12726 | (3) The debarment order applies from the date that the order is made
-- src:12727 | and continues in force until the Registrar cancels or suspends the
-- src:12728 | order.
@ref s 155B(3) (src:12726-12728)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the debarment order is made` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has cancelled the debarment order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has suspended the debarment order and the suspension operates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(3) the debarment order is in force` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the date the debarment order is made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The debarment order applies from the date that the order is made" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar has cancelled the debarment order` OR `the Registrar has suspended the debarment order and the suspension operates`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "continues in force until the Registrar cancels or suspends the order" -- the "until" is met (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (2) a person who has a debarment order made against him or her must not act as director of any company, except a company of which the person was a director
-- immediately before the order, or as secretary of any company, except one of which the person was secretary immediately before.
DECLARE `s 155B(2) what the person acts as` IS ONE OF
    `s 155B(2)(a) director of a company`
    `s 155B(2)(b) secretary of a company`

-- src:12710 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), a person who has a debarment order
-- src:12711 | made against him or her must not —
-- src:12716 | (a) except in respect of a company of which the person is a
-- src:12717 | director immediately before the order was made — act as
-- src:12718 | director of any company; or
-- src:12720 | (b) except in respect of a company of which the person is a
-- src:12721 | secretary immediately before the order was made — act as
-- src:12722 | secretary of any company.
@ref s 155B(2) (src:12710-12722)
GIVEN `the person has a debarment order made against him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debarment order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person acts as` IS A `s 155B(2) what the person acts as`
      `the person is a director of that company immediately before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a secretary of that company immediately before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(2) the subsection bars the person from acting as director or secretary of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has a debarment order made against him or her`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who has a debarment order made against him or her must not" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF NOT `the debarment order is in force`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "continues in force until the Registrar cancels or suspends the order" (subsection (3)) -- the "until" is met
          ELSE CONSIDER `what the person acts as`
               WHEN `s 155B(2)(a) director of a company` THEN
                    IF `the person is a director of that company immediately before the order was made`
                    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in respect of a company of which the person is a director immediately before the order was made" -- the "except" is met
                    ELSE JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 155B(2)(b) secretary of a company` THEN
                    IF `the person is a secretary of that company immediately before the order was made`
                    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in respect of a company of which the person is a secretary immediately before the order was made" -- the "except" is met
                    ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (4) the Registrar may cancel or suspend the order where the default has been rectified or on another prescribed ground, subject to conditions.
-- src:12732 | (4) The Registrar may, upon the application of a person who has a
-- src:12733 | debarment order made against the person or on the Registrar’s own
-- src:12734 | accord, cancel or suspend such debarment order where the default in
-- src:12735 | relation to the relevant requirements of this Act as at the time the
-- src:12736 | debarment order is made has been rectified or on such other ground as
-- src:12737 | may be prescribed, subject to such conditions as the Registrar may
-- src:12738 | impose.
@ref s 155B(4) (src:12732-12738)
GIVEN `the default in relation to the relevant requirements of this Act as at the time the debarment order is made has been rectified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another ground prescribed for cancelling or suspending the order applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(4) the Registrar may cancel or suspend the debarment order` MEANS
    IF `the default in relation to the relevant requirements of this Act as at the time the debarment order is made has been rectified` OR `another ground prescribed for cancelling or suspending the order applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may ... cancel or suspend such debarment order where the default ... has been rectified or on such other ground as may be prescribed" -- a "where" gate (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)) that fails; a "may" with a "where" gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

-- (8), (9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister; the appeal does not suspend the order.
-- src:12778 | (8) Any person who is aggrieved by a debarment order made under
-- src:12779 | subsection (1), or the Registrar’s refusal to cancel or suspend a
-- src:12780 | debarment order under subsection (4), may appeal to the Minister.
@ref s 155B(8) (src:12778-12780)
GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by a debarment order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by the Registrar's refusal to cancel or suspend a debarment order under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(8) the person may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the person is aggrieved by a debarment order made under subsection (1)` OR `the person is aggrieved by the Registrar's refusal to cancel or suspend a debarment order under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who is aggrieved by a debarment order ..., or the Registrar's refusal to cancel or suspend" names two occasions and says nothing of others (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- src:12784 | (9) An appeal under subsection (8) does not suspend the effect of
-- src:12785 | the debarment order.
@ref s 155B(9) (src:12784-12785)
GIVEN `an appeal under subsection (8) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(9) the appeal suspends the effect of the debarment order` MEANS
    IF `an appeal under subsection (8) has been made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal under subsection (8) does not suspend the effect of the debarment order"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of an appeal under subsection (8) only

-- (10) the offence of contravening (2).
-- src:12789 | (10) Any person who contravenes subsection (2) shall be guilty of
-- src:12790 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:12791 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:12792 | both.
@ref s 155B(10) (src:12789-12792)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(10) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Any person who contravenes subsection (2) shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element is unmet

@ref s 155B(10) (src:12789-12792)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 155B(10) penalty`
`s 155B(10) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 155B(10) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person contravenes subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 155B(10) penalty` OF 10000, 2 TIMES 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (2 TIMES 12 months) or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (11) the Registrar may publish the names and particulars of persons against whom a debarment order continues in force.
-- src:12796 | (11) The Registrar may from time to time prepare and publish, in
-- src:12797 | such form and manner as the Registrar may decide, the names and
-- src:12798 | particulars of the persons against whom a debarment order has been
-- src:12799 | made and which continues in force.
@ref s 155B(11) (src:12796-12799)
GIVEN `a debarment order has been made against the person and continues in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(11) the Registrar may publish the name and particulars of the person` MEANS
    IF `a debarment order has been made against the person and continues in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the names and particulars of the persons against whom a debarment order has been made and which continues in force" -- a grant ("may") limited to those persons (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (12) definitions: "debarment order" means a debarment order made under (1); "relevant requirement of this Act" has the meaning given by s 155(2); "secretary" means a secretary appointed under s 171.
-- src:12803 | (12) In this section —
-- src:12805 | “debarment order” means a debarment order made under
-- src:12806 | subsection (1);
-- src:12808 | “relevant requirement of this Act” has the meaning given by
-- src:12809 | section 155(2);
-- src:12811 | “secretary” means a secretary of the company appointed under
-- src:12812 | section 171.
@ref s 155B(12) (src:12803-12812)
GIVEN `the order is a debarment order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(12) "debarment order" the order is a debarment order` MEANS
    IF `the order is a debarment order made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“debarment order” means a debarment order made under subsection (1)" (a "means" definition)

@ref s 155B(12) (src:12808-12809)
GIVEN `the requirement is a relevant requirement of this Act as section 155(2) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(12) "relevant requirement of this Act" the requirement is a relevant requirement` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is a relevant requirement of this Act as section 155(2) gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant requirement of this Act” has the meaning given by section 155(2)" -- the whole definition is handed to that subsection, so a requirement that fails its test is not one

@ref s 155B(12) (src:12811-12812)
GIVEN `the person is a secretary of the company appointed under section 171` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155B(12) "secretary" the person is a secretary of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a secretary of the company appointed under section 171`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“secretary” means a secretary of the company appointed under section 171" (a "means" definition)

DECLARE `s 155B(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 155B(2)(a) act as director of a company other than one of which the person was a director immediately before the order was made`
    `s 155B(2)(b) act as secretary of a company other than one of which the person was secretary immediately before the order was made`

-- src:12710 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), a person who has a debarment order
-- src:12711 | made against him or her must not —
-- src:12716 | (a) except in respect of a company of which the person is a
-- src:12717 | director immediately before the order was made — act as
-- src:12718 | director of any company; or
-- src:12720 | (b) except in respect of a company of which the person is a
-- src:12721 | secretary immediately before the order was made — act as
-- src:12722 | secretary of any company.
@ref s 155B(2) (src:12710-12722)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 155B(2) act`
`s 155B(2)(a) a person with a debarment order must not act as director of another company` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 155B(2)(a) act as director of a company other than one of which the person was a director immediately before the order was made`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "a person with a debarment order acted as director of a company other than one of which the person was a director immediately before the order was made"

@ref s 155B(2)(b) (src:12720-12722)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 155B(2) act`
`s 155B(2)(b) a person with a debarment order must not act as secretary of another company` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 155B(2)(b) act as secretary of a company other than one of which the person was secretary immediately before the order was made`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "a person with a debarment order acted as secretary of a company other than one of which the person was secretary immediately before the order was made"

§ `Section 155C: disqualification under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`

DECLARE `s 155C(2) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 155C ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 155C section 59 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 155C section 60 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 155C section 61 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 155C none of these`

-- (1) subject to permission, a person subject to a disqualification or order under s 59, 60 or 61 of the LLP Act must not act as director of, or be concerned in the management of, any company or foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies, during the period.
-- src:12818 | 155C.—(1) Subject to any permission which the Court may give
-- src:12819 | pursuant to an application under subsection (3), a person who is
-- src:12824 | subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under
-- src:12825 | section 59, 60 or 61 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005
-- src:12826 | must not act as director of, or in any way (whether directly or
-- src:12827 | indirectly) take part in or be concerned in the management of, any
-- src:12828 | company or any foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11
-- src:12829 | applies during the period of disqualification or disqualification order.
@ref s 155C(1) (src:12818-12829)
GIVEN `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` IS A `s 155C ground`
      `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked is within the period of disqualification or disqualification order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155C(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` MEANS
    IF `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` EQUALS `s 155C none of these`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under section 59, 60 or 61 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (3)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to any permission which the Court may give pursuant to an application under subsection (3)" -- the permission was given
          ELSE (IF NOT `the date asked is within the period of disqualification or disqualification order`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the period of disqualification or disqualification order" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
                ELSE (IF `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING)))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any company or any foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies" names the bodies and says nothing of others

-- src:12835 | (2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:12836 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:12837 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:12838 | both.
@ref s 155C(2) (src:12835-12838)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155C(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 155C(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element is unmet

@ref s 155C(2) (src:12835-12838)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 155C(2) penalty`
`s 155C(2) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 155C(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person contravenes section 155C(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 155C(2) penalty` OF 10000, 2 TIMES 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (2 TIMES 12 months) or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (3) a person subject to a disqualification or order under s 59 or 61 may apply to the Court for permission, upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice.
-- src:12842 | (3) A person who is subject to a disqualification or disqualification
-- src:12843 | order under section 59 or 61 of the Limited Liability Partnerships
-- src:12844 | Act 2005 may apply to the Court for permission to act as director of,
-- src:12845 | or to take part in or be concerned in the management of, a company or
-- src:12846 | a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies during the
-- src:12847 | period of disqualification or disqualification order, upon giving the
-- src:12848 | Minister not less than 14 days’ notice of the person’s intention to
-- src:12849 | apply for such permission.
@ref s 155C(3) (src:12842-12849)
GIVEN `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` IS A `s 155C ground`
      `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` IS A DATE
      `the date the person applies to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155C(3) the person may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order`
    WHEN `s 155C section 59 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` THEN
         IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` `the date the person applies to the Court` 14 Days
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to the Court for permission ..., upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice" -- an "upon" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md
    WHEN `s 155C section 61 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` THEN
         IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` `the date the person applies to the Court` 14 Days
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the same "upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice" gate; split site (ii)
    WHEN `s 155C section 60 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under section 59 or 61 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005" names two sections and says nothing of section 60
    WHEN `s 155C none of these` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under section 59 or 61" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- src:12855 | (4) On the hearing of any application under subsection (3), the
-- src:12856 | Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the
-- src:12857 | granting of the application.
@ref s 155C(4) (src:12855-12857)
GIVEN `the hearing is of an application under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155C(4) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` MEANS
    IF `the hearing is of an application under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the hearing of any application under subsection (3), the Minister may be represented" -- an "on" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

§ `Section 155D: disqualification under the VCC Act`

DECLARE `s 155D(2) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 155D ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 155D section 56 of the VCC Act`
    `s 155D section 57 of the VCC Act`
    `s 155D section 58 of the VCC Act`
    `s 155D section 59 of the VCC Act`
    `s 155D section 60 of the VCC Act`
    `s 155D none of these`

-- src:12863 | 155D.—(1) Subject to any permission which the Court may give
-- src:12864 | pursuant to an application under subsection (3), a person who is
-- src:12865 | subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under
-- src:12866 | section 56, 57, 58, 59 or 60 of the VCC Act must not act as
-- src:12867 | director of, or in any way (whether directly or indirectly) take part in
-- src:12868 | or be concerned in the management of, any company or any foreign
-- src:12873 | company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies during the period of
-- src:12874 | the disqualification or disqualification order.
@ref s 155D(1) (src:12863-12874)
GIVEN `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` IS A `s 155D ground`
      `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked is within the period of the disqualification or disqualification order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155D(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` MEANS
    IF `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` EQUALS `s 155D none of these`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under section 56, 57, 58, 59 or 60 of the VCC Act" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (3)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to any permission which the Court may give pursuant to an application under subsection (3)" -- the permission was given
          ELSE (IF NOT `the date asked is within the period of the disqualification or disqualification order`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the period of the disqualification or disqualification order" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
                ELSE (IF `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING)))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any company or foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies" names the bodies and says nothing of others

-- src:12880 | (2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:12881 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:12882 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:12883 | both.
@ref s 155D(2) (src:12880-12883)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155D(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155D(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 155D(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element is unmet

@ref s 155D(2) (src:12880-12883)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155D(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 155D(2) penalty`
`s 155D(2) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 155D(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person contravenes section 155D(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 155D(2) penalty` OF 10000, 2 TIMES 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (2 TIMES 12 months) or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (3) a person subject to a disqualification or order mentioned in ss 56, 58, 59 and 60 of the VCC Act may apply to the Court for permission, upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice.
-- src:12887 | (3) A person who is subject to a disqualification or disqualification
-- src:12888 | order mentioned in sections 56, 58, 59 and 60 of the VCC Act may
-- src:12889 | apply to the Court for permission to act as director of, or to take part
-- src:12890 | in or be concerned in the management of, a company or a foreign
-- src:12891 | company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies during the period of
-- src:12892 | the disqualification or disqualification order, upon giving the
-- src:12893 | Minister not less than 14 days’ notice of the person’s intention to
-- src:12894 | apply for such permission.
@ref s 155D(3) (src:12887-12894)
GIVEN `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` IS A `s 155D ground`
      `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` IS A DATE
      `the date the person applies to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155D(3) the person may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` MEANS
    IF    (`the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` EQUALS `s 155D section 56 of the VCC Act`)
       OR (`the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` EQUALS `s 155D section 58 of the VCC Act`)
       OR (`the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` EQUALS `s 155D section 59 of the VCC Act`)
       OR (`the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order` EQUALS `s 155D section 60 of the VCC Act`)
    THEN (IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` `the date the person applies to the Court` 14 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to the Court for permission ..., upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice" -- an "upon" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "mentioned in sections 56, 58, 59 and 60 of the VCC Act" names four sections and says nothing of section 57 or of a person with no such disqualification

-- src:12900 | (4) On the hearing of any application under subsection (3), the
-- src:12901 | Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the
-- src:12902 | granting of the application.
@ref s 155D(4) (src:12900-12902)
GIVEN `the hearing is of an application under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155D(4) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` MEANS
    IF `the hearing is of an application under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the hearing of any application under subsection (3), the Minister may be represented" -- an "on" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

§ `Section 155E: debarment under the VCC Act`

DECLARE `s 155E(3) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (2) subsection (1) applies from the date the debarment order is made until the Registrar cancels or suspends the order.
-- src:12921 | (2) Subsection (1) applies from the date that the debarment order is
-- src:12922 | made until such time as the Registrar cancels or suspends the order.
@ref s 155E(2) (src:12921-12922)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the debarment order is made` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has cancelled the debarment order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has suspended the debarment order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155E(2) subsection (1) applies on the date asked` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the date the debarment order is made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies from the date that the debarment order is made" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar has cancelled the debarment order` OR `the Registrar has suspended the debarment order`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until such time as the Registrar cancels or suspends the order" -- the "until" is met (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 155E(1) what the person acts as` IS ONE OF
    `s 155E(1)(a) director of a company`
    `s 155E(1)(b) secretary of a company`

-- src:12908 | 155E.—(1) A person who has a debarment order made against him
-- src:12909 | or her under section 59 of the VCC Act must not —
-- src:12911 | (a) except in respect of a company of which the person is a
-- src:12912 | director immediately before the order was made — act as
-- src:12913 | director of any company; or
-- src:12915 | (b) except in respect of a company of which the person is a
-- src:12916 | secretary immediately before the order was made — act as
-- src:12917 | secretary of any company.
@ref s 155E(1) (src:12908-12917)
GIVEN `the person has a debarment order made against him or her under section 59 of the VCC Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) applies on the date asked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person acts as` IS A `s 155E(1) what the person acts as`
      `the person is a director of that company immediately before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a secretary of that company immediately before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155E(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as director or secretary of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has a debarment order made against him or her under section 59 of the VCC Act`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has a debarment order made against him or her under section 59 of the VCC Act must not" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF NOT `subsection (1) applies on the date asked`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies from the date that the debarment order is made until such time as the Registrar cancels or suspends the order" (subsection (2))
          ELSE CONSIDER `what the person acts as`
               WHEN `s 155E(1)(a) director of a company` THEN
                    IF `the person is a director of that company immediately before the order was made`
                    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in respect of a company of which the person is a director immediately before the order was made" -- the "except" is met
                    ELSE JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 155E(1)(b) secretary of a company` THEN
                    IF `the person is a secretary of that company immediately before the order was made`
                    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in respect of a company of which the person is a secretary immediately before the order was made" -- the "except" is met
                    ELSE JUST TRUE)

